  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating which lottery concentrates more probability on favorable outcomes (i.e., less negative ones), thus favoring Lottery B due to its higher 80% chance of zero and lower 20% chance of loss. The individual in the report acknowledges the higher probability (likely of zero) in one option and contrasts it with the smaller loss in the other, which aligns with considering the distribution of outcomes. This suggests awareness of the probability-weighted profile of the lotteries, which is related to skewness. However, the phrasing 'relatively smaller loss' indicates some pull toward the less severe loss (-3000), which is in Lottery A, the less left-skewed option. The individual does not clearly express a preference for concentration of probability on favorable outcomes as a guiding rule, nor do they conclude in favor of the more left-skewed lottery. The reasoning appears more trade-off-based between probability and magnitude, rather than distributional skew. Therefore, while some relevant information is considered (probabilities and outcomes), the rule of preferring the more left-skewed lottery is not clearly applied. The justification reflects a mixed consideration rather than adherence to the skewness rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 40
}

